  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.nhatrang.edu.vn/ontology/shrimp-disease">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="http://www.nhatrang.edu.vn/ontology/shrimp-disease/releases/1.1.0"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.1.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <dcterms:title xml:lang="en">Shrimp Disease Ontology (ShrimpOntology)</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:creator>Nha Trang University research team</dcterms:creator>
    <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-31</dcterms:created>
    <dcterms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-31</dcterms:modified>
    <dcterms:description>Relation-aware learning release with explicit recognition-state semantic anchors and alignment-role metadata for ontology-conditioned domain adaptation.</dcterms:description>
    <rdfs:comment>Release 1.0.0. Native OWL axioms and SWRL rules are intended to be reproducible in an OWL/SWRL-capable reasoning environment. Python procedures used for RDF mapping, orchestration, thresholding, UI, and SPARQL execution are not ontology entailments unless explicitly represented as SWRL/OWL axioms.</rdfs:comment>
    <dcterms:rights>License to be assigned by the authors before public release.</dcterms:rights>
    <sd:releaseNote>Audited legacy DATN.rdf: corrected FarmContext class/datatype-property collision; deprecated pondAge/salinity/waterTemperature as classes; migrated explicit disease logic to native OWL property chains and SWRL; retained Python-only procedures as metadata, not entailments.</sd:releaseNote>
    <sd:releaseNote>Release 1.1.0 adds RecognitionState anchors, hasSemanticAnchor/hasRecognitionState, alignmentRole/alignmentEligible metadata, semantic-anchor restrictions, and repairs SWRL numeric built-ins R13-R15. Provenance, context, evidence-management, and explanation relations are excluded from the OCRDA semantic alignment graph by default.</sd:releaseNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.nhatrang.edu.vn/ontology/shrimp-disease#alignmentRole">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>alignment role</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Role in the learning projection: semantic, provenance, context, evidence, explanation, or other.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
